## 5. YouTube title cleanup
Strip artifacts from YouTube titles during content extraction. Common patterns to remove:
- Leading "(NNN)" view/subscriber counts e.g. "(604)"
- " - YouTube" suffix at the end of titles

In `services/extractor.py`, clean the title after extraction:

```python
import re

def clean_title(title: str) -> str:
    # Remove leading (number) artifacts e.g. "(604) "
    title = re.sub(r'^\(\d+\)\s*', '', title)
    # Remove " - YouTube" suffix
    title = re.sub(r'\s*[-–]\s*YouTube\s*$', '', title, flags=re.IGNORECASE)
    return title.strip()
```

Call `clean_title()` on the extracted title before saving to DB.

